er ports.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd\nreasoning: The aux-service pod is failing due to a port conflict on port 8080. To confirm if another pod is using this port, I need to check all container ports across the namespace. This will reveal if any other service is inadvertently using port 8080, causing the conflict. The solution likely involves adjusting port configurations in the pod or service definitions. \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation -o jsonpath=\'{.items[*].spec.containers[*].ports}\'"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=1495, prompt_tokens=12729, total_tokens=14224, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc48-41c1-7811-b2b6-112e030016f4-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12729, 'output_tokens': 1495, 'total_tokens': 14224}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='0a298d76-8312-4138-9c3d-8cee297998a0')]]
