er ports.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd\nreasoning: The aux-service pod is failing due to a port conflict on port 8080. To confirm if another pod is using this port, I need to check all container ports across the namespace. This will reveal if any other service is inadvertently using port 8080, causing the conflict. The solution likely involves adjusting port configurations in the pod or service definitions. \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation -o jsonpath=\'{.items[*].spec.containers[*].ports}\'"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1495, 'prompt_tokens': 12729, 'total_tokens': 14224, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc48-41c1-7811-b2b6-112e030016f4-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12729, 'output_tokens': 1495, 'total_tokens': 14224}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='0a298d76-8312-4138-9c3d-8cee297998a0'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to figure out why the aux-service pod is crashing. The logs show an OSError about port 8080 being already in use. So the first thought is that another service is using port 8080, causing the aux-service to fail when it tries to bind to it.\n\nEarlier, they checked the services in the namespace and saw that aux-service is set to use port 8080. But maybe another pod is also using the same port. The user ran a command to get all container ports across the namespace. Let me check the output of that command.\n\nWait, the output from the kubectl get pods command with the jsonpath fo