Wait, the "spec" inside the template should have "containers" as an array. The structure should be:\n\n"spec": {\n  "template": {\n    "spec": {\n      "containers": [\n        { ... }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nSo the JSON should end with } after the "spec" in the template. But in the command, after the containers array, there\'s a closing } for the spec, then another } for the template, and another } for the main spec. Wait, maybe the JSON is missing a closing brace after the containers array. Let me see:\n\nThe part after "containers": [ ... ] should be closed with ] and then the } for the "spec" inside the template. Then the } for the template, and finally the } for the main spec. But in the command, after the containers array, there\'s a ] and then }} to close the spec and template. Wait, maybe the JSON is missing a closing brace after the containers array. Let me count the braces:\n\nOriginal JSON:\n\n"{\\"spec\\":{\\"template\\":{\\"spec\\":{\\"containers\\":[{\\"name\\":\\"aux-service\\",\\"ports\\":[{\\"containerPort\\":8081,\\"name\\":\\"http\\",\\"protocol\\":\\"TCP\\"}]}}]}}"\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n- "spec": { ... }\n  - "template": { ... }\n    - "spec": { ... }\n      - "containers": [ ... ]\n        - { ... } (container)\n      - ] (closing containers array)\n    - } (closing spec)\n  - } (closing template)\n- } (closing spec)\n\nWait, the "containers" array is closed with ] and then the } for the spec. Then the } for the template, and finally the } for the main spec. That seems correct. But the error is about an extra } after the array element. Maybe the JSON is missing a comma after the container in the containers array. Wait, the containers array has one element, so no comma needed. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the JSON is missing a closing brace after the "ports" array. Let me check the ports part:\n\n"ports": [\n  {\n    "containerPort": 8081,\n    "name": "http",\n    "protocol": "TCP"\n  }\n]\n\nThis is correctly closed with ] and the } for th