rvice\'s port configuration to make sure it\'s also updated. If the service is still on 8080, that could cause another conflict. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the user should use kubectl apply to update the deployment YAML, which might be more reliable. But since the user is restricted to non-interactive commands, using patch is the way to go. \n\nSo the next tool call should be to run the patch command again, ensuring the JSON is correctly formatted. Then, check the service\'s port configuration using get_services or another tool. If the service\'s port is still 8080, adjust that as well.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\nreasoning: The previous patch command did not update the container port to 8081. I need to reapply the patch with corrected JSON formatting to ensure the containerPort is set to 8081. This will resolve the port conflict.\n\ntool_call: {"command": "kubectl patch deployment aux-service -n hotel-reservation -p \'{\\"spec\\":{\\"template\\":{\\"spec\\":{\\"containers\\":[{\\"name\\":\\"aux-service\\",\\"ports\\":[{\\"containerPort\\":8081,\\"name\\":\\"http\\",\\"protocol\\":\\"TCP\\"}]}}]}}}\'"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 786, 'prompt_tokens': 4017, 'total_tokens': 4803, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc4b-3f5e-7531-8734-9260063646eb-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4017, 'output_tokens': 786, 'total_tokens': 4803}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='e02f7a10-4443-458f-80ed-56523b20869a'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to fix a port conflict on port 8080 